<%# ORPHANED as of 2026 Phase 3.2: `hujahs/_child_card` no longer renders this partial —
    the "Challenge to debate" affordance now links straight to the `debates#new` create
    page (rounds picker + opening argument), which also collects the stance this dialog
    used to. Left on disk rather than deleted per the Phase 3.2 task brief; nothing in
    `app/` currently references it. The rest of this comment describes the flow as it
    worked while it WAS wired up, kept for history rather than rewritten to a fiction.

    "Challenge to debate" control on an argument (child) card. Only rendered for a
    signed-in viewer who is NOT the argument's author (guarded by the caller).

    The <dialog> exists BEFORE any Debate does, so its element id is scoped to the
    argument — dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog) — NOT a debate. DebatesController's
    create.turbo_stream.erb closes it remotely with the exact same dom_id.

    Each opposing stance is its own button_to POST /hoojah/:slug/debates (params
    argument_id + challenger_stance) — the model enforces challenger_stance !=
    opponent_stance, and offering only the opposing stances keeps the pick valid by
    construction and works with JS off (plain form POST → the debate show page).

    Locals: argument (the child hoojah being challenged), hujah (the root hoojah),
    stance (the argument author's stance name, for the response-filter sync).

    DESIGN SYSTEM (Slice 9, Task 4.8) —
    docs/design-system/components/overlays/Dialog.prompt.md, plus
    CompactHujahCard.prompt.md for the trigger, which the design system calls
    `ChallengeLink` and which "renders below the card, never inside it". The panel was
    already the design system's dialog to the letter — 8px rounding, the large shadow,
    the 40% black backdrop, 448px max width, a hairline header carrying the title and an
    X — so the shell does not move, and neither does the header, the same markup
    `users/_profile_edit` carries. Dialog.prompt.md names all three of these ("Flag this
    hoojah, Challenge @user to a debate, Edit your profile") as one component, and the X
    in all three now comes from `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey")` — true
    again only after a follow-up, because Task 4.8 moved this one and the flag dialog's
    and left `users/_profile_edit` on the string it kept in Task 4.6. What changed:

    - The trigger and the X and Cancel controls all go through
      `ds_button_classes(variant: :link, ...)`, whose emitted string the trigger was
      already spelling by hand almost exactly. Almost, in full: against the retired
      hand-typed string the trigger picks up SIX utilities — `justify-center`,
      `transition`, `active:scale-95`, `disabled:opacity-50`, `disabled:cursor-default`,
      and an explicit `p-0`. Only the two press utilities are visible here; the other four
      are inert (the row has no free main-axis space to distribute, the button is never
      disabled, and preflight already zeroes a button's padding). That is the whole list —
      do not restate it as "just `transition` and `active:scale-95`". The variant itself is
      the bare borderless transparent text control: pink for the challenge affordance, grey
      for the two dismissals, which is Dialog.prompt.md's "bare grey Cancel". `text-xs`
      stays at the call site because `:link` deliberately carries no font size — this link
      is 12px, not the 16px it would otherwise inherit, and the helper's contract is that a
      link button inherits its context.
    - The stance rows lose the 1px edge and the rounding around each one, and the gap
      between them. That is the same correction Task 4.7 made to the two analytics
      surfaces, and the authority is readme.md's VISUAL FOUNDATIONS assigning the greys by
      job: "Tailwind grays for hairlines (`#f3f4f6`), field borders/tracks (`#e5e7eb`),
      hover fills (`#f9fafb`)". `#f3f4f6` is the HAIRLINE token — what `ui/_divider` spends
      INSIDE a surface — so a `border` in it drawn around the outside of one is off-token,
      and the per-row rounding was only softening a box that should not have been drawn.
      NOT because "rounding is forbidden": Card.prompt.md's rule is the narrow "Never round
      a feed card", and this design system rounds plenty else — readme.md gives dialogs
      `rounded-lg` and menus `rounded`, and `--radius: 4px` exists for small chrome. The
      `<dialog>` this list sits inside is itself `rounded-lg`. They do NOT become
      `ui/_card`s the way those two did — a card nested in a dialog is the second shadow
      the same rule rejects. What is left is the shared hairline between rows, which is
      also what makes this list and the flag dialog's reason list render identically at
      last: they are one component in the design system (`DialogChoiceList`) and were two
      different shapes in the app.
      Row padding is untouched, but unlike the flag dialog the rows do NOT sit exactly
      where they sat: this list was `flex flex-col gap-2`, so 8px of gap became a 1px
      hairline and rows two and three each rise about 7px. The flag dialog's list already
      drew a 1px rule between its rows (the `divide-<axis>` utilities in the hairline
      grey), so there it really was 1px for 1px and the same sentence is literally true —
      it is not here. (Spelled `divide-<axis>` on purpose: Tailwind scans this file as
      text, and the concrete class would put a rule back in the bundle that no view asks
      for.)

    FROZEN: `dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog)`, which `debates/create.turbo_stream.erb`
    closes remotely; `data-response-filter-target` / `data-response-filter-vote` on the
    wrapper, which the response filter matches by string against the copies in
    `_response_filter` and `_child_card`; every `data-*` on the trigger and the dialog;
    the POST to /hoojah/:slug/debates with argument_id + challenger_stance; and every word
    of copy — spec/system/debate_spec.rb clicks "Challenge to debate" and "Argue Agree" by
    name. %>
<% stance_labels = {1 => "Agree", 2 => "Neutral", 3 => "Disagree"} %>
<% opponent_stance = argument.vote %>
<div data-controller="dialog"
     data-response-filter-target="item"
     data-response-filter-vote="<%= stance %>"
     class="flex justify-end -mt-1 mb-1 pr-2">
  <button type="button" data-action="dialog#open"
          class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "neutral") %> text-xs">
    <%= lucide_icon("swords", class: "w-3.5 h-3.5") %> Challenge to debate
  </button>

  <dialog id="<%= dom_id(argument, :challenge_dialog) %>"
          data-dialog-target="dialog"
          data-action="click->dialog#backdropClose close->dialog#restoreFocus"
          aria-labelledby="dialog-title-challenge-<%= argument.id %>"
          class="rounded-lg shadow-lg p-0 w-full max-w-md backdrop:bg-black/40">
    <div class="flex items-center justify-between px-4 py-3 border-b border-gray-100">
      <h5 id="dialog-title-challenge-<%= argument.id %>" class="text-lg font-medium m-0">
        Challenge @<%= argument.user.username %> to a debate
      </h5>
      <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close" aria-label="Close"
              class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">
        <%= lucide_icon("x", class: "w-5 h-5") %>
      </button>
    </div>

    <div class="p-4">
      <p class="text-sm text-grey mb-3">
        They argued <strong><%= stance_labels[opponent_stance] || "their side" %></strong>.
        Pick the side you'll argue — you move first.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col">
        <% ([1, 2, 3] - [opponent_stance]).each_with_index do |cs, i| %>
          <%= render "ui/divider" unless i.zero? %>
          <%= button_to "/hoojah/#{hujah.slug}/debates",
                params: {argument_id: argument.id, challenger_stance: cs},
                class: "w-full text-left px-4 py-3 hover:bg-gray-50 bg-card cursor-pointer" do %>
            Argue <strong><%= stance_labels[cs] %></strong>
          <% end %>
        <% end %>
      </div>
      <div class="text-right mt-4">
        <button type="button" data-action="dialog#close"
                class="<%= ds_button_classes(variant: :link, tone: "grey") %>">Cancel</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </dialog>
</div>
